                            // When Qt is about to trigger an application Shortcut (or
                            // when WM/desktop is about to claim a key combo via Qt's
                            // shortcut routing), it first sends a ShortcutOverride
                            // event to the focused item. If we accept it, Qt cancels
                            // the shortcut and delivers the keystroke as a normal
                            // KeyPress to us instead. This is what lets Konsole
